\n  Categories: Classic fantasy\n  Description: While Aragorn, Merry, Pippin, and Gandalf battle Saruman's forces, Frodo and Sam struggle to get the ring to the fire that will destroy it.\n\nBook 3:\n  ISBN-13: 9780007136834\n  Title: And Then There Were None\n  Categories: Fiction\n  Description: Ten... Ten strangers are lured to an island mansion off the Devon coast. Over dinner, an unseen voice accuses each of them of harbouring a guilty secret, and by the end of the evening one of their number is dead. Nine... Their host fails to appear, and as the weather changes the island becomes a sinister and claustrophobic place to be stranded. Eight... Haunted by an ancient nursery rhyme, they all realise that the murderer is not only among them but is preparing to strike again. Seven... The tension escalates as the survivors try to keep one step ahead of their ingenious stalker, who seems be\n\nBook 4:\n  ISBN-13: 9780007145348\n  Title: Echo Burning\n  Categories: Fiction\n  Description: While hitchhiking through Texas, ex-military policeman Jack Reacher is picked up by a woman in need of protection from her abusive husband, who is about to be released from prison.\n\nBook 5:\n  ISBN-13: 9780007149520\n  Title: The Age of Wonder\n  Categories: Biography & Autobiography\n  Description: Shortlisted for the Samuel Johnson Prize and winner of the Royal Society Prize for Science Books, Richard Holmes's dazzling portrait of the age of great scientific discovery is a groundbreaking achievement. 'The Age of Wonder' is Richard Holmes's first major work of biography in over a decade. It has been inspired by the scientific ferment that swept through Britain at the end of the eighteenth century, 'The Age of Wonder' and which Holmes now radically redefines as 'the revolution of Romantic Science'. The book opens with Joseph Banks, botanist on Captain Cook's first Endeavour voyage, steppi\n\nBook 6:\n  ISBN-13: 9780007154852\n  Title: While the Light Lasts\n  Categories: Fiction\n  Description: Some of Agatha Christie's earliest stories - including her very first - which show the Queen of Crime in the making... A macabre recurring dream ... revenge against a blackmailer ... jealousy, infidelity and a tortured conscience ... a stolen gemstone ... the haunting attraction of an ancient relic ... a race against time ... a tragic love triangle ... a body in a box ... an unexpected visitor from beyond the grave... Nine quintessential examples of Agatha Christie's brilliance are contained in this new collection of early short stories - including the very first one she ever wrote - and provi\n\nBook 7:\n  ISBN-13: 9780007155002\n  Title: Mind Maps at Work\n  Categories: Business & Economics\n  Description: Tony Buzan has used his patented Mind Maps system to teach millions of people around the world how to unlock the infinite creativity of the human mind. Now he presents a practical guide to achieving workplace success and satisfaction.\n\nBook 8:\n  ISBN-13: 9780007157150\n  Title: Out of the Silent Planet\n  Categories: Fiction\n  Description: Dr Ransom, a Cambridge academic, is abducted and taken on a spaceship to Mars. His captors are plotting to plunder the planet's treasures and plan to offer Ransom as a sacrifice to the creatures who live there. Ransom discovers he has come from the Earth. This is the first novel in CS Lewis' classic sci-fi trilogy.\n\nBook 9:\n  ISBN-13: 9780007157174\n  Title: That Hideous Strength\n  Categories: Fiction\n  Description: Mark is enticed to join a group called N.I.C.E. which aims to control all human life. His wife is having bizarre prophetic dreams about a decapitated scientist. As Mark is drawn into the sinister group he finds the truth of his wife's dreams. The book ends in a battle with the powers of Hell.\n\nBook 10:\n  ISBN-13: 9780007157600\n  Title: The Elder Gods\n  Categories: Fiction\n  Description: New series, new world, and a glorious story destined to reach the biggest audience yet. They are called the Dreamers. They look like sleeping children. They are, in fact, Gods. There are eight elder Gods, four awake, four asleep, by turns. When they sleep, they sleep for eons. The only time the Gods are vulnerable is when the sleepers awake. Knowing this, the Ruler of the Wasteland, ambitious to become a God by destroying Gods, watches and waits, marshalling troops for war. So it is that the coming of the Dreamers passes unnoticed in the Wasteland. But the world is soon out of kilter, it is be\n\n\nRemember:\n- Vary query length (short / medium / long)\n- Do not repeat the book title\n- Focus on themes, emotions, plot, and characters\n", 'role': 'user'}], 'model': 'gpt-4o-mini', 'response_format': {'type': 'json_schema', 'json_schema': {'schema': {'$defs': {'BookQueries': {'description': 'Structured output for queries generated for a single book.\n\nThe LLM is asked to produce queries of varying lengths to simulate\ndifferent user search behaviours.', 'properties': {'isbn13': {'description': 'ISBN-13 of the source book these queries were generated for.', 'title': 'Isbn13', 'type': 'string'}, 'queries': {'description': 'List of search queries relevant to the book. Should include short (1-3 words), medium (4-8 words), and long (9+ words) queries.', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'title': 'Queries', 'type': 'array'}}, 'required': ['isbn13', 'queries'], 'title': 'BookQueries', 'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False}}, 'description': 'Structured output returned by the LLM for a batch of books.\n\nWrapping in a single batch call reduces API round-trips and token overhead.', 'properties': {'books': {'description': 'One BookQueries entry per book in the input batch.', 'items': {'$ref': '#/$defs/BookQueries'}, 'title': 'Books', 'type': 'array'}}, 'required': ['books'], 'title': 'BatchQueryResponse', 'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False}, 'name': 'BatchQueryResponse', 'strict': True}}, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.0}}
